# The caster's own graveyard holds no creature card (an Entomb for a Lightning Bolt), so Bot1 puts nothing and is asked
# nothing (the refused Choose), while Bot2, whose graveyard holds an Ornithopter, still puts it onto the battlefield (its only creature card, which the unscripted answer takes):
# Exhume is symmetrical, not "you return a creature".

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Exhume
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Lightning Bolt
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Swamp x8
Ornithopter
Swamp x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot1.Search(Lightning Bolt)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot2.Search(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Exhume.Cast
! Bot1.Choose
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Swamp
Bot2.Battlefield = Swamp; Ornithopter
